      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "According to the 2011 Census, India's population reached 121.08 crore, making it the second most populous country globally at the time.",
        "Uttar Pradesh is the most populous state in India, whereas Sikkim has the lowest population among all states.",
        "Kerala recorded the highest literacy rate at 94.00% and the highest sex ratio at 1084 females per 1000 males.",
        "Bihar has the highest population density of 1,106 persons per sq km, while Arunachal Pradesh has the lowest density at 17 per sq km.",
        "The decadal growth rate of India's population during 2001-2011 was 17.70%."
      ],
      "id": "w1tsldh"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The first non-synchronous Census was conducted in 1872 under Lord Mayo, while the first synchronous Census was conducted in 1881 under Lord Ripon.",
        "The year 1921 is celebrated as the 'Great Divide' in demographic history due to a negative decadal growth rate of -0.31%.",
        "Nagaland was the only Indian state to record a negative decadal population growth (-0.58%) in the 2011 Census.",
        "Dadra and Nagar Haveli recorded the highest decadal population growth rate among Union Territories at 55.88%."
      ],
